      "note": "A human runs this. On a terminal, `yojo` prompts on stderr and reads the personal access token with no echo. In automation, a human pipes the secret on stdin with `--token-stdin`; a secret is never an argument, file, or environment variable. The credential is stored per base URL, so `--base-url` alone can reuse it later.",
